00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:06.239 align:start position:0%
in north-central Thailand nestled  amongst lush green mountaintops sits  five striking white Buddha's and mosaics  that glitter against the landscape  located a five hour drive north of  Bangkok is what house horn Khao also  known as temple of the glass cliff this  relatively new structure was completed  in 2004 and named an official temple in  2010 the temple features five Buddhas  all in meditation pose in descending in  size much like a Russian doll they  represent the five Buddha's who visited  the earth according to Hindu tradition  [Music]  in addition to the Buddha's this modern  structure also includes a 5 level pagoda  shaped like a lotus flower the  surrounding surfaces are covered with  around 5 million mosaic tiles stones and  pottery all in vibrant colors  the site is remote and only accessible  by private car or tour but the journey  to this peaceful colorful modern Oasis  is well worth the journey  [Music]
 

